8072858b18cfb5376dd226c8e5c3d8ec4a41d9902e4186f6290d","file":"preprints/A-single-lattice-covering-bound-of-order-n-log-n-September-23-2026/build/overview.tex","line":16,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"44f3f4552b91388b17a4ff01f528f8542bed5fdd627660e24e94b8302aa6d1fa","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-single-lattice-covering-bound-of-order-n-log-n-September-23-2026/build/overview.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:461285133b5f8072858b18cfb5376dd226c8e5c3d8ec4a41d9902e4186f6290d","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-single-lattice-covering-bound-of-order-n-log-n-September-23-2026/build/overview.tex#L16"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere is an absolute constant $C>0$ such that, for every integer\n$n\\ge2$ and every convex body $K\\subset\\R^n$, one full-rank lattice\n$\\Lambda$ satisfies\n\\[\n K+\\Lambda=\\R^n,\\qquad\n \\frac{\\vol_n(K)}{\\det\\Lambda}\\le Cn\\log n.\n\\]\nNo symmetry or boundary regularity is assumed."}
